{
 "contract": "desk_card",
 "version": 2,
 "supersedes": null,
 "covers": "what a TICKET row renders as — the control it offers, whether anybody is counted as waiting on it, and what it says where a control is absent. ADDITIVE TO v1, which is untouched: v1 covers desk recommendation/request rows and their nine states; v2 covers the highway's ten lifecycle states. Neither binds a count; the stage contract binds the count.",
 "rules_version": "ticket card v2 (2026-08-26)",
 "producing_module": "src/app/clark/studio/desk/ticketCard.ts::ticketCardState",
 "clarkharness_copy": "OWED. v1 is checked in to both repos byte-identical and regenerated by ClarkHarness's scripts/gen_desk_contract.py. This dispatch is KryptonPay-only, so the ClarkHarness copy of v2 and its generator entry do not exist yet and v2 binds ONE repo until they do.",
